[Home](Home.oot) [Start](Use.oot) [Language](Language.oot) [Commands](Options.oot) [Packages](Packages.oot) [Capabilities](Safety.oot) [Active Defense](Morpher.oot) [How it works](Limits.oot) [Pay](Pay.oot)

## 1. What it is

openOODA is a systems language. You write `.oo` files.
The product path typechecks the file, emits C through `chs_rt`, compiles with host `gcc`, and runs.

An effect needs a capability token. No token, no effect.
`oodac` is the compiler. `ooda` is the driver.

Linux x86_64 is the first-machine install. See [Start](Use.oot).

## 2. Three rules

### Authority

A process does not get file, net, or exec rights by default.
A function that does an effect takes a token, for example `&FsReadCap`.
Missing or forged tokens fail closed. See [Capabilities](Safety.oot).

### Binary defense

`emit-c` is the everyday emit. Binary defense is on by default.
Use `--plain` or `--debug` to turn it off. See [Active Defense](Morpher.oot).

### Small tools

Read a small slice of a file. Use `outline`, `reflect`, `fix`, and `patch`.
Do not dump a full emit. See [Commands](Options.oot).

## 3. Product path

```
.oo source  ->  ooda check  ->  emit-c (chs_rt)  ->  gcc  ->  run
```

1. `ooda check` typechecks. Const `requires` / `ensures` fold here.
2. `emit-c` writes C for `chs_rt`. Defense stays on unless you opt out.
3. Host `gcc` builds the native binary.
4. At run, Landlock and `setrlimit` apply when you pass `&SysCap`.

Read more: [How it works](Limits.oot).

## 4. What this pin adds

v0.209.0 keeps the C path as product.
The standard library packs PostgreSQL v3 StartupMessage and Query.
MySQL packs handshake v10, COM_QUERY, OK, and ERR. ERR is not OK.
RESP recovers Simple String, Error, Integer, Bulk String, and Array.
The SQL lexer emits SELECT and WHERE and refuses garbage.
A B-tree splits full nodes. A missing key is not found.
A Bloom filter never reports an inserted key as absent.
LRU evicts the least-recent key. A skip list stays ordered.
vec2 and vec3 compute dot, cross, magnitude, lerp, and reflection.
look_at and perspective are not identity. Translate then invert recovers a point.
An R-tree overlap and nearest-neighbor query hit the inserted box.
A convex hull has a positive area.
Gaussian, Sobel, and Laplacian change pixels.
A biquad low-pass and high-pass differ on a DC step.
Linear and sinc resample change length with the sample-rate ratio.
HTTP/2, WebSocket, DNS, MQTT, ChaCha20-Poly1305, Ed25519, Shamir, TOTP, BLAS, LU, QR, ELF, Huffman, and LZ77 stay in the library.

Leftover methods stay `ERR\tc_emit`. Device GPU dispatch stays residual.
LLVM, WASM, and x86 emits are extra. They are not the everyday path.

